   ],
   "missing_before": [],
   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "This is the classic Ralstonia solanacearum defined minimal (MP/MM) medium: only four salts plus glucose. R. solanacearum is prototrophic, so there is no separate trace-element cocktail or vitamin mix - iron is supplied solely by FeSO4-7H2O and sulfate is shared by the Fe/ammonium/Mg sulfates. The current ion-level components (Fe2+, glucose, K+, Mg2+, NH4+, phosphate, sulfate, O2) were already complete; this record re-expresses them as the actual source compounds with concentrations. Cells were pre-grown/adapted in BG medium (glucose 5 g/L, bactoagar 15 g/L) then transferred to this minimal med"
  },
